-- title:
--   Irreducible components at infinity of the normalized projective closure
-- statement:
--   Let $W_0=V(p)\subseteq\mathbb A^N$ for a prime ideal $p\subseteq F[x_1,\dots,x_N]$, let $W\subseteq\mathbb P^N$ be its projective closure, $H_\infty=V(x_0)$ the hyperplane at infinity and $\nu:\widetilde W\to W$ the normalization. This module defines:
--
--   1. the homogenization $f^h=x_0^{\deg f}f(x_1/x_0,\dots,x_N/x_0)$ and the ideal $p^h$ generated by the $f^h$, $f\in p$, the homogeneous ideal of $W$;
--   2. the homogeneous coordinate ring $S=F[x_0,\dots,x_N]/p^h$ of $W$;
--   3. the integral closure $\widetilde S$ of $S$ in its fraction field, the homogeneous coordinate ring of $\widetilde W=\operatorname{Proj}\widetilde S$;
--   4. the set of minimal primes of the ideal $x_0\widetilde S$, which are the irreducible components of $D_\infty=\nu^{-1}(W\cap H_\infty)$.
--
--   These objects state Theorem 7.3.
--
--   **Formalization Note** $\operatorname{Proj}\widetilde S\to\operatorname{Proj}S$ is finite and birational with normal source, so it is the normalization; $\nu^{-1}(V_+(x_0))=V_+(x_0\widetilde S)$, whose irreducible components are $V_+(P)$ for the minimal primes $P$ of $x_0\widetilde S$, of dimension $\dim\widetilde S/P-1$. The variable $x_0$ is `none`, and $x_i$ is `some (i-1)`.
-- source:
--   A. Dey, P. Dutta, Z. Guo, An Exponential Top Fan-In Hierarchy for Border Depth-4 Circuits, STOC 2027 submission (manuscript sha256 518aaf99…), §7.1 (Projective Space; Normalization), pp.77–78; Theorem 7.3, p.80

import Mathlib
set_option autoImplicit false

open MvPolynomial

namespace BorderD4.Supplement

variable {F : Type*} [Field F] {N : ℕ}

/-- The homogenization `f^h(x_0, x_1, …, x_N) = x_0^{deg f} f(x_1/x_0, …, x_N/x_0)` of `f ∈ F[x_1, …, x_N]`; the
variable `x_0` is `none` and `x_i` is `some (i − 1)`. -/
noncomputable def homogenize (f : MvPolynomial (Fin N) F) : MvPolynomial (Option (Fin N)) F :=
  ∑ α ∈ f.support,
    monomial (Finsupp.mapDomain Option.some α + Finsupp.single none (f.totalDegree - α.degree)) (coeff α f)

/-- The ideal `p^h ⊆ F[x_0, …, x_N]` generated by the homogenizations of the elements of `p`. For a prime
`p = I(W_0)` over an algebraically closed field it is the homogeneous ideal of the projective closure `W ⊆ P^N`
of `W_0` (Cox–Little–O'Shea, Ch. 8, §4, Theorem 8). -/
noncomputable def homogenizeIdeal (p : Ideal (MvPolynomial (Fin N) F)) : Ideal (MvPolynomial (Option (Fin N)) F) :=
  Ideal.span (homogenize '' (p : Set (MvPolynomial (Fin N) F)))

/-- The homogeneous coordinate ring `S = F[x_0, …, x_N]/p^h` of the projective closure `W` of `W_0 = V(p)`. -/
abbrev projCoordRing (p : Ideal (MvPolynomial (Fin N) F)) : Type _ :=
  MvPolynomial (Option (Fin N)) F ⧸ homogenizeIdeal p

/-- The integral closure `S̃` of `S = projCoordRing p` in its fraction field: the (graded) homogeneous coordinate
ring of the normalization `W̃ = Proj S̃` of `W = Proj S`. -/
abbrev normalizedCone (p : Ideal (MvPolynomial (Fin N) F)) : Type _ :=
  integralClosure (projCoordRing p) (FractionRing (projCoordRing p))

/-- The irreducible components of `D_∞ = ν^{-1}(W ∩ H_∞)`, for `W ⊆ P^N` the projective closure of `W_0 = V(p)`,
`H_∞ = V(x_0)` the hyperplane at infinity and `ν : W̃ → W` the normalization, as prime ideals: the minimal primes of
the ideal `x_0 S̃` of the homogeneous coordinate ring `S̃` of `W̃`.
Source: Dey, Dutta, Guo, An Exponential Top Fan-In Hierarchy for Border Depth-4 Circuits, STOC 2027 submission (manuscript sha256 518aaf99…), §7.1 "Projective Space" and "Normalization", pp.77–78, and Theorem 7.3, p.80.

**Formalization Note** `W̃ = Proj S̃`, where `S̃` is the integral closure of `S = F[x_0, …, x_N]/p^h` in its
fraction field: `S̃` is a graded domain, finite over `S`, its homogeneous localizations are normal, and
`Proj S̃ → Proj S` is finite and birational, so it is the normalization. `ν^{-1}(V_+(x_0)) = V_+(x_0 S̃)`, whose
irreducible components are `V_+(P)` for the minimal primes `P` of `x_0 S̃` (these are homogeneous; when
`dim W_0 ≥ 1` they have height one and so are relevant), and `dim V_+(P) = dim S̃/P − 1`. -/
noncomputable def componentsAtInfinity (p : Ideal (MvPolynomial (Fin N) F)) : Set (Ideal (normalizedCone p)) :=
  (Ideal.span {algebraMap (projCoordRing p) (normalizedCone p)
    (Ideal.Quotient.mk (homogenizeIdeal p) (X none))}).minimalPrimes

end BorderD4.Supplement


